    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0540" n="420" xml:id="pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">813.00 Tacoma/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schuyler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-14T10:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 14,
                                1922—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:30
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>78. I had a long talk with the President yesterday and he assured me of his
                    [acceptance] in principle of the invitation to the proposed conference if it
                    could be postponed long enough to make it possible and prudent for him to
                    attend. His departure from this capital just now even if possible under the
                    existing political situation, which it is not, would cause wild reports of his
                    flight and refuge on a United States ship especially if I accompanied him. This
                    should be avoided for conditions here are delicate. …</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
